# For more information on these fields, see:
# https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/adding_to_third_party.md#readme_chromium
#
# TaffyGo owns this directory. It is vendored under //taffy rather
# than under //third_party/android_deps on purpose, and the reason is recorded
# in docs/decisions/0031-one-tree-and-dependency-injection.md: android_deps
# commits no jars (its DEPS entries pin CIPD packages in a namespace a fork
# cannot publish to) and the roller regenerates its build files, which is the
# clobber shape OD-076 has recorded four times. Nothing here edits an upstream
# file, so a Chromium roll cannot touch it.
#
# Every jar below is byte-identical to the artifact Maven Central serves for the
# coordinate named in its block. The Gradle and GN builds both use Dagger
# 2.60.1 from the version owned by gradle/libs.versions.toml, so both builds run
# the same processor over the same sources.
#
# Two of the sixteen reach a device; the other fourteen run on the build host
# inside kapt and are never dexed. Each block says which it is in its Shipped
# field, and tools/lib/vendored_assets.py holds every checksum against
# vendor/dagger.txt.

Name: Dagger
Short Name: dagger
URL: https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/com/google/dagger/dagger/2.60.1/dagger-2.60.1.jar
Version: 2.60.1
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: Apache-2.0
License File: LICENSE
Shipped: yes
Security Critical: no
CPEPrefix: unknown

Description:
The dependency-injection runtime: Provider, Lazy, MembersInjector and the
generated factories' base types. Reaches the device.

Local Modifications:
None.
-------------------- DEPENDENCY DIVIDER --------------------

